[node name="Palather" type="Label3D" parent="Man"]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, -0.465602, 0.331211, 0.00664306)
pixel_size = 0.001
modulate = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
text = "CYBER CITY RUN(1)                                  User Commands                                CYBER CITY RUN(1)

NAME
       cyber-city-run - collect system critical data pending reboot

SYNOPSIS
       cyber-city-run  -hv|-bcEeHiOSs1 -d secs -n max -u|U user -p pids -o field -w [cols]

       The traditional switches `-' and whitespace are optional.

DESCRIPTION
       The user  controls their avatar  with a dynamic  real-time view of the running system. The avatar can be dir-
       ected via the WASD keys or ARROW keys in combination with \"mouse look\" to navigate a virtual system abstract-
       ion layer known as \"CYBER CITY\". OPTIONAL: SHIFT key acceleration, \"m\" for \"MUTE\", and \"ALT-ENTER\" fullscreen 

       The abstraction provides  a limited interactive  interface for data collection  and  manipulatory operations.
       The  extended   physical  metaphoric  interface  displays system  summary  information as well  as a familiar
       mapping  to  \"real world\" construction.   Though encompassing  possible physical models  the mapping  remains
       imperfect. Notably, vertically  aligned surfaces provide only a surface level tangibility lacking solidity.

       The  cyber-city-run   program  represents  a data retrieval of  final resolution in the (unlikely) event of a
       data breach. The consciousness  of the user  is leveraged via avatistic  representation   to enable  critical
       archival operational facilities on an \"as needed basis\", memoriamatizationally speaking. 

       Pragmatically  the simulation  expands with  infinite  vastness. Advanced system  access granted  pending layer
       data typing as managed by the  system  kernel.   The types  of  system  summary  information  shown  and the 
       types, order and size of information displayed for processes are all user manipulable and as such acquisition
       will be made persistent across reboots.

       This  program  is  provided by  Loose Bit Labs.  Textures  are  custom   shader   based  excluding the avatar.
       Shout  out  to  jarble  on  shadertoy  for inspiring part  of the floor shader (WljcRG). Character  animation
       via   mixamo, modelling  and texturing  by YT & Blender.  CYBER CITY RUN is  written  using Godot. Music via
       Zen_Man (https://pixabay.com/users/zen_man-4257870): 
       -        https://pixabay.com/music/techno-trance-melodic-techno-03-extended-version-moogify-9867/
       -        https://pixabay.com/music/techno-trance-background-loop-melodic-techno-01-2490/
	      The  program  provides a  limited  interactive interface  for data retrieval simulated experientials for most 
       1337 HA><><ORZ of all ages, ethnicities, creeds, genders, political affiliations, phsyical, mental, and moral 
       competencies or so you might well imagine though no such warranty is implied as far as you know.
<EOF>"
